untably generated-filter DCT; complete-space interval FTC; symmetric-order Fubini with both s-finite measures; RCLike convex mean-value bound; continuous compact-support integrability with measurable opens and finite measure on compacts; compact-image upper bound; real-parameter inner-product differentiation; symmetric second Fréchet derivative with the full minSmoothness threshold; finite-measure constant integrability with finite extended norm; and sigma-finite coordinate-product splitting. M003's selected declaration is integral_prod_symm from the later successful probe, not the initially considered integral_prod. All native structural premises are retained in source statements/obligations and specialized to standard real Euclidean and Lebesgue structures. No literature theorem E is imported, so the exercise citation is target provenance rather than an unverified theorem assumption. The AND graph has only H/M roots, one producer per N/P, and every retained M/N belongs to P's dependency closure. Structural validation is not a mathematical verdict; these are my same-author checks under nl0-audit-a-8, not independent Audit A.\",\"readiness\":\"no_known_issue\",\"open_issues\":[],\"resolutions\":[],\"output_notes\":[{\"id\":\"N001\",\"note\":\"Read N001 independently of its producer. Its full pointwise tangency and acceleration orthogonality are established in R001/S001-S002 from H004/H005 and the product rule. The conditional scalar formula retains its universal scalar meaning, without any differentiation of a. R001/S003 proves and exports smoothness of e, the exact commuting mixed derivatives and the complete e_t formula with coefficients 2. Thus R003 needs neither a remembered equation label nor an unexported calculus fact from R001.\"},{\"id\":\"N002\",\"note\":\"R002/S001-S006 prove the entire quantified statement, including compatible C,R,B for each t0, the original time interval J, C strictly inside Q, all positive derivatives zero outside C at interior times, the finite box measure, the full list of continuous integrable spatial terms, and the uniform |e_t| bound on Q×[3t0/4,5t0/4]. R002/S006 closes t0 to obtain all-time integrability. The output gives R003 and R004 their actual support and finiteness information without requiring the producer body.\"},{\"id\":\"N003\",\"note\":\"R003/S001 bounds the absolute quotient for both signs of h, with η=t0/4. S002 supplies an integrable whole-space indicator bound. S003 proves the actual punctured-filter limit of integrals by M001; S004 identifies those integrals with the difference quotient of D004 using integrability, not a formal differentiation of an undefined integral. The output exports differentiability, the exact derivative representation, the full e_t expression and finiteness, for every t0>0.\"},{\"id\":\"N004\",\"note\":\"R004/S001 gives the exact product derivative for g. S002 proves the integral of that derivative is zero by endpoint FTC, explicit measure-preserving coordinate splitting, and the correct Fubini integration order, including n=1. S003 transfers the integrable supported terms to ℝ^n, applies linearity, dot-product symmetry and subtraction. This proves the complete exported identity with its minus sign and both finite integrals, quantified in t0 and j.\"},{\"id\":\"P\",\"note\":\"R005/S001 substitutes N004 into the complete N003 formula and combines the finite spatial sum into Δ_xu exactly as defined. S002 uses N001 to make the resulting integrand zero and combines N002/N003 to give integrability, actual finite energy and differentiability at every strictly positive time. S003 applies the zero-bound case of M004 to get E(b)=E(a), including equal endpoints. D003-D004 supply the unchanged energy normalization and no assertion at time zero. The exported conclusion covers the whole selected target, with constancy as the supplied proof's additional consequence.\"}],\"inference_notes\":[{\"id\":\"R001\",\"dependency_and_local_assumption_check\":\"Inspected th