gy, guarded by N002, proved without using E. Every E-using inference R003 and R005 directly receives N002, and every use of the derivative definitions directly receives H002. The five units follow all supplied phases: R001 tangency, explicit scalar equation and density derivative; R002 common support/integrability and compact uniform bound; R003 mean-value bound and dominated difference-quotient limit; R004 coordinate FTC and Fubini integration by parts; R005 cancellation and constancy. No supplied needed calculation or limiting step was omitted; the optional explicit wave-map equation was retained as well. M001-M010 were compared with actual successful native probes and official pinned source reads: countably generated-filter DCT; complete-space interval FTC; symmetric-order Fubini with both s-finite measures; RCLike convex mean-value bound; continuous compact-support integrability with measurable opens and finite measure on compacts; compact-image upper bound; real-parameter inner-product differentiation; symmetric second Fréchet derivative with the full minSmoothness threshold; finite-measure constant integrability with finite extended norm; and sigma-finite coordinate-product splitting. M003's selected declaration is integral_prod_symm from the later successful probe, not the initially considered integral_prod. All native structural premises are retained in source statements/obligations and specialized to standard real Euclidean and Lebesgue structures. No literature theorem E is imported, so the exercise citation is target provenance rather than an unverified theorem assumption. The AND graph has only H/M roots, one producer per N/P, and every retained M/N belongs to P's dependency closure. Structural validation is not a mathematical verdict; these are my same-author checks under nl0-audit-a-8, not independent Audit A.\",\"readiness\":\"no_known_issue\",\"open_issues\":[],\"resolutions\":[],\"output_notes\":[{\"id\":\"N001\",\"note\":\"Read N001 independently of its producer. Its full pointwise tangency and acceleration orthogonality are established in R001/S001-S002 from H004/H005 and the product rule. The conditional scalar formula retains its universal scalar meaning, without any differentiation of a. R001/S003 proves and exports smoothness of e, the exact commuting mixed derivatives and the complete e_t formula with coefficients 2. Thus R003 needs neither a remembered equation label nor an unexported calculus fact from R001.\"},{\"id\":\"N002\",\"note\":\"R002/S001-S006 prove the entire quantified statement, including compatible C,R,B for each t0, the original time interval J, C strictly inside Q, all positive derivatives zero outside C at interior times, the finite box measure, the full list of continuous integrable spatial terms, and the uniform |e_t| bound on Q×[3t0/4,5t0/4]. R002/S006 closes t0 to obtain all-time integrability. The output gives R003 and R004 their actual support and finiteness information without requiring the producer body.\"},{\"id\":\"N003\",\"note\":\"R003/S001 bounds the absolute quotient for both signs of h, with η=t0/4. S002 supplies an integrable whole-space indicator bound. S003 proves the actual punctured-filter limit of integrals by M001; S004 identifies those integrals with the difference quotient of D004 using integrability, not a formal differentiation of an undefined integral. The output exports differentiability, the exact derivative representation, the full e_t expression and finiteness, for every t0>0.\"},{\"id\":\"N004\",\"note\":\"R004/S001 gives the exact product derivative for g. S002 proves the integral of that derivative is zero by endpoint FTC, explicit measure-preserving coordinate splitting, and the correct Fubini integration order, including n=1. S003 transfers the integrable supported terms to ℝ^n, applies linearity, dot-product symmetry and subtraction. This proves the complete exported identity with its minus sign and both finite integrals, quantified in t0 and j.\"},{\"id\":\"P\",\"note\":\"R005/S001 substitutes N004 into the complete N003 formula and combines the finite spatial sum into Δ_xu exactly as defined. S002 uses N001 to make the resulting integrand zero and combines N002/N003 to give integrability, actual finite energy and differentiability at every strictly positive time. S003 applies the zero-bound case of M004 to get E(b)=E(a), including equal endpoints. D003-D004 supply the unchanged energy normalization and no assertion at time zero. The exported conclusion covers the whole selected target, with constancy as the supplied proof's additional consequence.\"}],\"inference_notes\":[{\"id\":\"R001\",\"dependency_and_local_assumption_check\":\"Inspected the current R001 packet. S001 uses H002 to differentiate the coordinate curves and H004 to differentiate their locally constant squared norm; M007 yields 2u·u_t=0 and its spatial analogue, exported as F001. In S002 the scalar witness is chosen only from direct H005; its sole role is algebraic substitution. Differentiating the already global zero identities with H002/M007 gives u·u_tt=−|u_t|² and u·∂jj u=−|∂j u|², and H004 gives the scalar coefficient. S003 uses H002 for smoothness closure, M008 for the actual mixed-derivative interchange, and M007 for the two square derivatives before taking the finite sum. The real dot-product identities are directly finite component algebra. The scalar witness does not escape: F002 is scalar-universal and the final statement quantifies its scalar condition. Arbitrary x,t and the spatial index are closed; there are no additional undischarged assumptions or hidden support hypotheses.\",\"source_application_check\":\"Checked R001/A001-A004 against the packet's M007 and M008 contracts. M007 uses K=ℝ and V=ℝ^m, whose standard structures satisfy all native premises. The time and spatial coordinate derivatives for both factors are supplied by H002 at the displayed interior points; S001 explicitly provides zero extensions of time curves when the native theorem needs total curves on ℝ, with identical germs at positive times. Its conclusion is the derivative of the dot product; real symmetry then gives the displayed factors of 2. For the second differentiation the identically zero functions are F001, not merely zero at one point. M008 uses the local representative of u on ℝ^n×ℝ, order 2, and minSmoothness ℝ 2=2; H002 provides C² at the positive-time point. Evaluation of its symmetric bilinear second derivative on the time and coordinate directions is exactly the two mixed partials used next. No derivative or regularity of the normal scalar is used.\",\"declaration_check\":\"Checked /graph/inferences/0/locals and S001-S003. x∈ℝ^n and t>0 are arbitrary and remain in scope through the last use. The arbitrary spatial index j is explicitly introduced for coordinate arguments, with its binder closed when passing to all indices and the finite sum. F001's universally bound index is alpha-renamed ℓ and does not shadow that local. The chosen a is available from H005 at (x,t), lives only in S002, and neither F002 nor the output depends on its private identity. The pointwise scalar binder α in F002 is separate. Curve parameters, sum indices and Fréchet directions are expression-bound or explicitly specified source instantiations. D002/D003 are usable because H002 is a direct input.\"},{\"id\":\"R002\",\"dependency_and_local_assumption_check\":\"Inspected R002's complete packet at candidate 3; its unchanged mathematical packet is retained at candidate 5. S001 instantiates H006 at the legitimate endpoints t0/2 and 3t0/2. S002 obtains a norm bound from compact C, including the empty case. S003 defines R=max(1,L+1), so |x_j|≤|x|≤L<R and R>0; the product box has exactly the finite measure displayed. S004 gives the actual local constancy argument on the open complement of closed C, so every positive derivative vanishes there; H002 supplies continuity, compact support follows by closure inside C, and M005 proves integrability of all listed terms. Its bounded-integral estimate is consistent with M006 and finite |Q|. S005 bounds |e_t| on a compact product wholly inside positive times, and S006 takes B=max(0,B0). Each existential choice has an earlier basis. H001 is used for the positive finite dimensional setup; H003 is not silently imported. No geometric or PDE assumption beyond these direct inputs is used and all witnesses are closed in the existential output.\",\"source_application_check\":\"R002/A001 and A003-A004 apply M006 with real ordered codomain. The norm on compact C is continuous; the spatial Q is compact as a finite product of compact intervals; the space-time box in S005 is compact and lies within the smooth domain. The finite scalar bounds therefore follow from the exact bounded-image conclusion, without presupposing a nonempty C or an extremizer. R002/A002 applies M005 to ℝ^n with its usual Borel/Lebesgue structures, finite on compact sets, and real-valued sections. S004 establishes continuity from H002 and support closure contained in closed compact C before the source call. This is the exact hypothesis needed for compact-support integrability, not literal compact support of u. Routine closure, compact-product and Euclidean-measure facts are standard basic applications with conditions displayed; no separate core project theorem is being assumed.\",\"declaration_check\":\"Checked t0,J and the sequence C,L,R,Q,B0,B in /graph/inferences/1/locals. F001 precedes the choice of C; F002 precedes the choice of L; R and Q are explicit expressions with positivity verified; F005 precedes B0 and B. In particular the corrected B0 basis is F005, not F004. C,R,J,Q stay live through S006, and each function section and index in F004 is explicitly quantified. The output quantifies all local witnesses, and e is used only with direct H002. E is not used in this guard-producing inference.\"},{\"id\":\"R003\",\"dependency_and_local_assumption_check\":\"Inspected the current R003 packet using only H002, N001, N002 and the three sources. S001 chooses the joint witnesses from N002 at the arbitrary t0 and η=t0/4, so both t0+h and the entire real segment lie strictly in J for 0<|h|<η. N001 exports the needed actual e_t derivative; N002 supplies its uniform bound and zero densities outside Q. The absolute quotient inequality is valid for either sign of h. S002 proves integrability of the indicator majorant. S003 uses the explicit total F with harmless off-germ values, its eventual continuity/integrability, pointwise derivative limit and the earlier F001-F002, and obtains the integral limit. S004 uses only nearby positive times and linearity for known integrable sections to identify this limit with the difference quotient of the guarded finite E. Every listed input has this role; no producer body or transitive H is being imported.\",\"source_application_check\":\"M004 is used with the zero-extended real function r↦e(x,r) and S=[3t0/4,5t0/4]; its derivative on this positive interval is exactly the N001 derivative. N002 gives the bound B for x∈Q, the endpoint inequalities give membership and convexity, and division uses |h|>0. M009 uses the finite-measure Q and finite real B, yielding integrability for the restriction; extension by zero on measurable Q gives the whole-space bnd. M001 is the countably generated filter version, not just a sequential theorem: the punctured neighborhood filter has the displayed countable basis. The six recorded grounds match its structural, measurability, domination, integrable-bound and almost-everywhere limit requirements one for one. The resulting limit of integrals is precisely F003; only then is integral linearity used to derive differentiability.\",\"declaration_check\":\"Checked /graph/inferences/2/locals and S001-S004. t0 is arbitrary positive; C,R,B are chosen compatibly from one existential N002 instance. Q and η are explicit definitions. bnd is introduced at S002 before use in S003, and F is introduced at S003 with a definition at every real h, avoiding any off-domain evaluation of e. Parameters x,h,r appearing in pointwise or curve arguments are bound in those expressions/statements, not escaping witnesses. F001-F003 export their quantifiers fully. N002 is a direct guard for E and H002 is a direct guard for e and the component derivative conventions.\"},{\"id\":\"R004\",\"dependency_and_local_assumption_check\":\"Inspected the current R004 packet after the coordinate-identification revision. S001 uses H002 and N002 to define smooth g, prove it vanishes near the boundary, and obtain the exact product derivative with integrable summands. F001 is available to S002. For each fixed remaining coordinate vector, FTC applies on the full closed interval because the line restriction is smooth also at endpoints; its two endpoint values vanish outside C. S002 then defines the actual splitting map and insertion inverse, invokes M010 to transport the restricted product measure and the integrable derivative, and invokes the selected symmetric-order Fubini theorem to integrate x_j first. The equality of the finite product of restrictions with restriction to the box is the ordinary rectangle-product identification, with all finite measures displayed. The empty remaining coordinate product for n=1 has mass one, so no missing dimensional case remains. S003 uses vanishing outside Q and linearity for integrable functions to obtain the full-space equality and its minus sign. No unexplained boundary decay or integral limit is substituted for compact support.\",\"source_application_check\":\"M007 receives the two jth-coordinate curves u_t and ∂j u, with their derivatives from direct H002; its dot-product derivative is F001 after real symmetry. M002 receives the scalar line restriction of g, endpoints −R,R and complete codomain ℝ; F001 gives differentiability and continuous derivative, hence interval integrability. M010 receives d=n−1 and restricted real coordinate measures, each finite of mass 2R and hence sigma-finite; the given spatial-index condition implies n=(n−1)+1 and a valid zero-based selected index. Its actual map is split with insertion inverse, so the measure-preserving conclusion grounds the transport rather than a guessed coordinate change. M003 is explicitly integral_prod_symm: first factor is coordinate j and its inner integral is the FTC integral, while the other coordinates form the outer factor. Both measures are finite and its transformed integrand is integrable by F001 plus M010 transport. Its source conclusion is therefore exactly the zero box integral used in S003.\",\"declaration_check\":\"Checked /graph/inferences/3/locals. t0 and j are arbitrary in their displayed ranges; C and the compatible R come from direct N002 before Q and g are defined. g is real-valued and defined on all spatial ℝ^n at the fixed positive t0. split is introduced in S002 only, with the ordered remaining coordinates and explicit insertion inverse; n≥1 follows from j's legitimate range, not an absent H. Its existence is explicit finite coordinate data and its measure property comes from M010. The fixed remaining coordinates in the line integration are universally chosen within their box and never escape. F001-F002 contain all local identities needed later; R's final output closes t0 and j and no private C,R,Q,g or split appears free.\"},{\"id\":\"R005\",\"dependency_and_local_assumption_check\":\"Inspected R005 as a conditional implication from the complete direct N statements and H002. In S001 N002 supplies finiteness and the E guard; N003 supplies actual differentiability and the exact derivative representation; N004 is summed only over the finite spatial indices. Linearity gives the displayed difference of integrals, and D002 combines it into u_t·(u_tt−Δ_xu) with the correct factor 2. H002 supplies all derivative-definition guards. S002 uses precisely the pointwise orthogonality clause exported in N001, not its proof body, to set this integrand to zero. Universal introduction yields F002 with no residual assumptions. S003 derives constancy for arbitrary positive endpoints by M004, including equal endpoints. There is no new PDE, no regularity assumption on a scalar and no claim at time zero.\",\"source_application_check\":\"The only direct native source use is M004 in S003, instantiated over ℝ with f a local extension of E, c=0 and the interval S=[min(a,b),max(a,b)]. F002 proves actual differentiability at every time of S and derivative zero; positivity of a,b proves the whole interval is contained in the domain. The ordinary interval inequalities prove convexity and both memberships. Thus its exact bound |E(b)−E(a)|≤0|b−a| is available and implies equality. The other factual steps are direct applications of the complete N001-N004 statements and elementary finite algebra plus basic integral linearity for the expressly integrable summands.\",\"declaration_check\":\"Checked t0's S001-S002 scope and a,b,S in S003. t0 is arbitrary positive and is closed before constancy. a,b are arbitrary positive reals; S is explicitly defined from them in the locals ledger and in the paragraph before the M004 call. The integration variables and finite sum indices are expression-bound. All uses of E have direct N002 and all derivative guards have direct H002; the local extension used by the source agrees near every point of S. P quantifies its remaining times/endpoints and contains no private witness or interval.\"}]}","status":"completed"}],"error":null,"incomplete_details":null,"tools":[{"type":"function","name":"search_mathlib","description":"在固定 mathlib 的 Lean 源码中搜索正则表达式，返回至多 100 行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"query":{"type":"string"}},"required":["query"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_mathlib","description":"读取固定 mathlib 中一个 Mathlib/...lean 文件的指定行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start_line":{"type":"integer"},"line_count":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start_line","line_count"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"search_external_sources","description":"Follow source-retrieval.md: arxiv first (default; an exact arXiv ID is allowed), then google title/author search, then google title/author DOI search, then scihub with a confirmed DOI. Use browser:true for normal local-browser readback of JavaScript/verification pages. Results and DOI strings are locators, not source/theorem approval. Record failed access and continue conditionally when the original stays unavailable.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"query":{"type":"string"},"engine":{"type":"string","enum":["arxiv","google","scihub"]},"browser":{"type":"boolean"}},"required":["query"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_external_source","description":"Read and retain a public HTTPS source and its hash-bound access record. Use offset to continue cached text. Retry with browser:true for a normal isolated local Chrome session if HTTPS needs JavaScript or verification. The optional browser uses ordinary site controls; unsupported challenges remain explicit failures. Verify full PDF identity, version, theorem and context yourself.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"url":{"type":"string"},"offset":{"type":"integer"},"limit":{"type":"integer"},"browser":{"type":"boolean"}},"required":["url"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"defer_primary_source","description":"After actual unavailable primary-source access, preserve a complete exact secondary quotation as an explicitly unverified external assumption. The statement must match the quote in a supplied input. Returns the verification record for E.source.verification; this never grants ordinary Audit A PASS.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"source_id":{"type":"string"},"statement":{"type":"string"},"input_id":{"type":"string"},"quote":{"type":"string"},"attempts":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}}},"required":["source_id","statement","input_id","quote","attempts"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_task_input","description":"Read one declared frozen document. For JSON use pointer (empty string lists the root); large objects return keys, and strings resume with offset=next_offset. For text use inclusive start/end lines and column=next_column when continuing a long line. Every serialized result is at most 32 KiB. Follow has_more and the returned continuation coordinates; no arbitrary local files are accessible.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"},"column":{"type":"integer"},"pointer":{"type":"string"},"offset":{"type":"integer"},"limit":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["id"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_yui","description":"Read declared Yui rules/templates; no tests, historical runs or personal files.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"},"column":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start","end"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"check_artifact","description":"Check a JSON artifact against the explicit stage contract; this is not automatic mathematical certification.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"submit_artifact","description":"Submit a JSON artifact after its stage checks.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"report_obstacle","description":"Report only a real substantive/suspected mathematical GAP, unavailable source or conflicting original input, with all five located fields. Ordinary unfinished NL0, source registration and JSON bookkeeping are not reports: continue an actual lookup or draft edit. TASK_INCOMPLETE is unavailable for NL0 authoring. Difficulty or a long run is not evidence of a mathematical gap.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"status":{"type":"string","enum":["SUBSTANTIVE_GAP","SUSPECTED_GAP","SOURCE_UNAVAILABLE","MISSING_SOURCE_STATEMENT","INPUT_CONFLICT"]},"location":{"type":"string"},"explanation":{"type":"string"},"basis":{"type":"string"},"partial_progress":{"type":"string"}},"required":["status","location","explanation","basis","partial_progress"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"check_draft","description":"Preferred structured-object form of check_artifact: provide artifact as an actual JSON object, not an escaped JSON string. Same complete validation and acceptance scope.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true}},"required":["artifact"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"submit_draft","description":"Preferred structured-object form of submit_artifact: provide artifact as an actual JSON object, not an escaped JSON string. Same complete validation and acceptance scope.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true}},"required":["artifact"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"probe_library","description":"Query a proved Mathlib theorem and its exact signature/axioms in the offline sandbox. Returns located evidence for an M source; the mathematical statement and applicability still require review. The optional module locator uses dotted syntax (Mathlib.Topology.Basic), never a slash path; omit it if unknown.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"declaration":{"type":"string"},"module":{"type":"string"}},"required":["id","declaration"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"find_library_sources","description":"Search pinned foundational metadata by an exact declaration name or ordinary mathematical terms. Ranked lexical candidates are not a theorem whitelist or an applicability judgment. Selected sources still need explicit M roots and complete checks.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"query":{"type":"string"}},"required":["query"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_draft","description":"Read a JSON pointer in your own same-stage candidate after an actual structural check. No other file/stage is accessible. For an existing string optionally supply both start_line/end_line to request up to 250 numbered lines and its complete text_sha256 for replace_lines. A read end beyond the text returns the remaining existing lines and actual range; the start must exist. Edits never clamp their range.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"candidate":{"type":"integer"},"pointer":{"type":"string"},"start_line":{"type":"integer"},"end_line":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["candidate","pointer"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_author_packet","description":"Same-author closing inspection of one structurally valid own conditional inference: exact direct inputs, output, declarations and own proof. No ancestor bodies, extra H, independent reviewer or Audit A feedback.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"candidate":{"type":"integer"},"inference":{"type":"string"}},"required":["candidate","inference"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"record_author_checks","description":"Save actual same-author notes and readiness against shared Audit A criteria. Unresolved/not-checked partial notes can be saved, but only complete actual packet inspection with no known issue can release a proof. Open issues persist until explicit located resolutions. No PASS or mathematical verdict is generated; independent Audit A receives none of these notes.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"candidate":{"type":"integer"},"original_context_note":{"type":"string"},"readiness":{"type":"string","enum":["no_known_issue","unresolved","not_checked"]},"open_issues":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"criterion":{"type":"string"},"location":{"type":"string"},"note":{"type":"string"}},"required":["id","criterion","location","note"],"additionalProperties":false}},"resolutions":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"location":{"type":"string"},"note":{"type":"string"}},"required":["id","location","note"],"additionalProperties":false}},"output_notes":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"note":{"type":"string"}},"required":["id","note"],"additionalProperties":false}},"inference_notes":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"dependency_and_local_assumption_check":{"type":"string"},"source_application_check":{"type":"string"},"declaration_check":{"type":"string"}},"required":["id","dependency_and_local_assumption_check","source_application_check","declaration_check"],"additionalProperties":false}}},"required":["candidate","readiness","open_issues","original_context_note","output_notes","inference_notes"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false}],"tool_choice":"auto","parallel_tool_calls":false,"prompt_cache_key":"84f65a9a-140e-48c9-8473-bd6a8d4f6d1c","prompt_cache_re